# Registry block media (images & video)

Use this when a block needs raster images (PNG, JPG, WebP) or video (MP4, WebM). Most blocks (navbars, SVG-only sections, etc.) do not need this.

## How it works

Media is served directly from `https://uiception.com`. There is no download step, no manifest file, and no `instrumentation.ts`. Consumers install a block and media works immediately with zero configuration.

## Consumer install

```bash
npx shadcn@latest add "https://uiception.com/r/<block-id>.json"
```

That's it. No extra setup required.

## Authoring: adding media to a block

### 1. Reference the CDN URL directly in the component

Use `https://uiception.com/images/blocks/<block-id>/` or `https://uiception.com/videos/blocks/<block-id>/` directly in the component file.

**`next/image`** — add `unoptimized` so consumers don't need `remotePatterns` in their `next.config`:

```tsx
import Image from "next/image"

export function MyBlockImage() {
  return (
    <Image
      src="https://uiception.com/images/blocks/my-block/my-block-bg.png"
      unoptimized
      alt=""
      fill
    />
  )
}
```

**Plain string constant** (shader props, video `src`, template helpers):

```tsx
// shader or other non-next/image usage
const BG = "https://uiception.com/images/blocks/my-block/my-block-bg.png"

// video
const VIDEO = "https://uiception.com/videos/blocks/my-block/screen-demo.mp4"

// template helper for multiple files
const avatar = (filename: string) =>
  `https://uiception.com/images/blocks/my-block/${filename}`
```

### 2. No manifest, no registryDependency

- Do **not** create a `media-manifest.json` file.
- Do **not** add `https://uiception.com/r/uiception-media-fetch.json` to `registryDependencies`.
- Do **not** list binary files (`public/images/…`, `public/videos/…`) in `registry.json`.

### 3. Ensure the asset is hosted

The binary must exist at `https://uiception.com/images/blocks/<block-id>/…` (or `/videos/…`) before going live. Place the file in `public/images/blocks/<block-id>/` on the authoring repo — Vercel serves it from there.

## Where assets live in this repo

```
public/images/blocks/<block-id>/
  <block-id>-bg.png

public/videos/blocks/<block-id>/
  screen-demo.mp4
```

## What NOT to do

| ❌ Old pattern (removed) | ✅ New pattern |
|---|---|
| `media-manifest.json` in block folder | Hardcode `https://uiception.com/…` in component |
| `registryDependencies: ["…/uiception-media-fetch.json"]` | No dependency needed |
| Local path `/images/blocks/…` in component | Absolute CDN URL `https://uiception.com/images/blocks/…` |
| `next/image` without `unoptimized` on external URL | Add `unoptimized` prop |
